{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R36 is placed across VOUTP and VOUTN with schematic value '24k', and the SPICE deck models it as 24k, but its MPN/description identify a 24Ω 0805 resistor (FRC0805J240TSD).",
      "expected": "R36 should be a 24k resistor (PoE detection/bleeder across the PoE-derived rails); the BOM/MPN must match the 24k value.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"219\") (name \"VOUTN\") ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"1\") ... ) ... (net (code \"220\") (name \"VOUTP\") ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"2\") ... )"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R36 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the BOM/MPN is used for assembly, a 24Ω resistor is placed across the PoE input instead of 24k. At 48V this would dissipate about 96W, likely damaging the resistor and preventing correct PoE detection/loading.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D14", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D14.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "Net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D4, D14 and D23; there is no supply, driver, jumper or other component connected to this net.",
      "expected": "The LED anodes should be connected to a valid 3.3V LED power source (for example +3V3 or the switched LED power net) so the PI activity and Ethernet indicator LEDs can illuminate.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "D4 (PI activity), D14 (Ethernet LEDY) and D23 (Ethernet LEDG) have no anode supply and will never light.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5", "U10.8", "U11.8"],
      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN"],
      "observed": "Both GND1 and GND2 pins of the isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 are tied to the same GND net. Their bus-side VCC2 pins are powered from 5V_switched_CAN, which is generated from the non-isolated main +5V rail.",
      "expected": "For isolated CAN buses, the bus-side GND2 should be a separate isolated ground and VCC2 should come from an isolated supply, keeping CAN-side ground isolated from logic/power ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"5V_switched_CAN\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation of both CAN buses is defeated. The CAN bus side shares ground and a non-isolated 5V supply with the logic, so ground loops and common-mode noise can couple between the CM4 board and motor controllers.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain supported anomalies: R36 is specified as 24k in value/SPICE but sourced as 24Ω, the LED power net for D4/D14/D23 is floating, and the isolated CAN transceivers' grounds are tied together. These would cause PoE signature/current issues, dead indicator LEDs, and loss of CAN isolation."
}

